Fonts for Folio
===============

PDFs usually carry their own fonts. When one doesn't (and for ebooks in
scripts Folio has no font for, such as Chinese, Japanese and Korean), Folio
looks for a font on your computer through fontconfig:

- With PackMan's FontConfig (UnixFC) installed, Folio uses its fonts and
  settings, like other programs that use fontconfig. Fonts installed with
  PackMan (into UnixFont:truetype) are found there.
- Without it, Folio uses the TrueType and OpenType fonts (.ttf, .otf, .ttc)
  you put in this folder.

For Chinese, Japanese and Korean, the Noto Sans CJK or Droid Sans Fallback
fonts (both free, SIL Open Font Licence / Apache) work well.

The first time Folio needs a font after new ones are added, it takes a
moment to look through them; what it finds is kept in
<Choices$Write>.Folio.FontCache (or UnixFC's own cache).
